From: Asdlerto Korry <korryasdlerto@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] m52xq: simple: set up pipeline links without trusting the cached flags

A second libcamera instance (libcamerasrc in Snapshot for 4K next to
wireplumber) changes links behind the back of the first one, so the
cached MEDIA_LNK_FL_ENABLED is stale: an old link stays enabled and camss
returns -EBUSY for the new one (msm_csiphy3 -> msm_csid0), or a needed
link is not re-enabled. Always disable the other non-immutable links and
always enable the pipeline link (the kernel ignores unchanged flags).
---
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -798,8 +798,16 @@
 				if (link == sinkLink)
 					continue;
 
-				if ((link->flags() & MEDIA_LNK_FL_ENABLED) &&
-				    !(link->flags() & MEDIA_LNK_FL_IMMUTABLE)) {
+				/*
+				 * m52xq: do not trust the cached ENABLED flag. Another
+				 * libcamera instance (libcamerasrc in an application next
+				 * to the one in wireplumber) may have enabled a link on
+				 * this entity since our media graph was enumerated: the
+				 * cache still says "disabled", the link stays on and camss
+				 * refuses the new one (csid link_setup: -EBUSY). Disabling
+				 * an already disabled link is a no-op in the kernel.
+				 */
+				if (!(link->flags() & MEDIA_LNK_FL_IMMUTABLE)) {
 					ret = link->setEnabled(false);
 					if (ret < 0)
 						return ret;
@@ -807,7 +815,11 @@
 			}
 		}
 
-		if (!(sinkLink->flags() & MEDIA_LNK_FL_ENABLED)) {
+		/*
+		 * m52xq: enable the pipeline link even when the cache says it is
+		 * enabled - another libcamera instance may have disabled it.
+		 */
+		if (!(sinkLink->flags() & MEDIA_LNK_FL_IMMUTABLE)) {
 			ret = sinkLink->setEnabled(true);
 			if (ret < 0)
 				return ret;
